window.docContents[25].resolve({"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___--Environment":{"contents":"Most functions in this library are in the Env monad, built on top of the EnvT monad transformer.\n\nThe environment monad transformer.\n\nBe careful that, in practice, EnvT works on monads that lift BaseIO, hence the definition of\nEnv:\n\nThe environment monad.\n\nThe only way to run Env-code is through its run functions.\n\n\nMost types in the Cvc library take an implicit instance of the Ω class.\n\n#check Ω\n\n\n#check Env.run\n\n\nCvc.Env.run {α : Type} (code : [inst : Ω] → Env α) : BaseIO (Res α)\n\n\nvariable [Ω]\n\n\ndef codeInEnv : Env Unit :=\n  println! \"running in the cvc5 environment\"\n\n#eval Env.runIO codeInEnv\n\n\nrunning in the cvc5 environment\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Environment and  Ω","header":"1.1. Environment","id":"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___--Environment"}});